                  "stem": "Add -ed to a word and write a sentence.",
                  "type": "WRITING_TASK",
                  "page_ref": "p.30"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "listening": {
          "section_name": "Listen and Respond",
          "transcript_ref": "p. 260",
          "transcript_file": "knowledge_commons/textbooks/english/ix/transcript.pdf",
          "transcript_unit": "Unit 1",
          "transcript_text": "Speaker 1: I like places of nature that offer comfort. As an elderly man, I love visiting serene riversides. I still remember my last visit to Poicha village on the bank of river Narmada. The gentle flow of the river spoke to my soul. I could reflect, meditate, and find inner harmony. Riverside visits are my favourite; I have tickets booked for Ayodhya next. Speaker 2: Adventures thrill me — there's no place better than the mountains. A visit to the Western Ghats changed it all for me. Our college supports adventure sports and the mountains are my playground. Speaker 3: I'm a photographer. I find the deserts breath-taking. Vast stretches of sand dunes and the colours of the desert before sunset combined with the play of shadows is matchless — the desert's beauty rewards me with one-of-a-kind clicks. Speaker 4: I love the mountains but my heart beats for the forests of India. As a travel vlogger, exploring biodiverse areas allows me to share the wonders of nature. My recent trip was to the Sundarbans.",
          "tasks_verbatim": [
            {
              "task_text": "You will listen to four people talk about the places they like to travel to. As you listen, write the speaker number for the two pictures given. (Transcript for teacher on page 260) [Picture 1: person hiking with backpack; Picture 2: person rock-climbing]",
              "question_bank": [
                {
                  "stem": "Picture 1 (hiker with backpack) — Speaker No. ___",
                  "type": "FILL_IN",
                  "page_ref": "p.30"
                },
                {
                  "stem": "Picture 2 (rock climber) — Speaker No. ___",
                  "type": "FILL_IN",
                  "page_ref": "p.30"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "task_text": "You will once again listen to the four speakers. As you listen, match the given statements to the speaker. There are two statements that you do not need. [Statements: 1. The green surroundings look beautiful visually. 2. The group visits make even the difficult areas seem easy. 3. The quietness of the environment here leads to a peaceful experience. 4. The risk and thrill in such an area is what is most appealing. 5. The dry expanse promises to appeal to the spirit of exploration. 6. The sight of such beauty is very inviting and has to be captured.]",
              "question_bank": [
                {
